{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && git status --short && rg -n -i \\\"P60R|semifiniteness|full.corner\\\" <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md || true && sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/lean-proof/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"lean/stabilizer\n M PLAN.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\n M work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/UltraweakNormality.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? aristotle_tasks/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\n2472:- Let `p=zq`. A faithful trace finite on the corner identity `p` makes `p` finite in `pMp` and hence in `M`: any `v` with `v^*v=p` and `vv^*<p` has `v=pvp\\in pMp`; traciality gives equal trace values while faithfulness gives `tau(p-vv^*)>0`, a contradiction. Normality is unnecessary; semifiniteness alone is insufficient. Local sources: Blackadar V.2.1.14, PDF p. 446; Kadison--Ringrose II Definition 6.3.1, PDF p. 41. [Task 2]\n2475:- The ambient-corner bridge is exact, not an inclusion shortcut: `(zq)M_Gamma(zq)=(zq)(zM_Gamma)(zq)`. Apply the corner-finiteness lemma in ambient `zM_Gamma` to `p=zq`; the restricted object is a faithful positive tracial functional, not necessarily a normalized state. Blackadar III.1.1.5 (printed p. 237/PDF p. 245) supplies central carrier/support; do not conflate it with C*-ideal “full corner.” [Task 5]\n2510:- for this stabilizer project, retain `G_F=G\\cap A_F` and broad proof-compatible conditional framing; do not turn a semifiniteness certificate into factoriality or type-`II_\\infty` classification [Task 1]\n2516:- Treat the support-corner-to-semifiniteness argument as a separate frontier: strong/strong-* topology, bicommutants, Kaplansky density, ultraweak normality, finite projections/central support, and full-finite-projection-implies-semifinite are not an integrated finished package. Defer central direct-integral/factor classification. Suggested staged interfaces: `finite_stabilizer_density_and_partial_trace`, `support_monotonicity_from_compatible_projector_states`, `abstract_support_corner_is_tracial`, `full_finite_projection_implies_semifinite`. [Task 1]\n---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n---\nname: lean-proof\ndescription: Use when asked to prove something in Lean. Covers one-step-at-a-time proving, error priority, working on the hardest case first, proof cleanup, and handling dependent type rewriting issues.\n---\n\n# Lean Proof Methodology\n\nThese are non-negotiable constraints for writing Lean proofs correctly.\n\n## One Step at a Time\n\nWrite one tactic, check diagnostics (use `done` to see unsolved goals), repeat. Never write multiple tactics before checking.\n\n**`by sorry` is acceptable**: For placeholders you're not actively working on.\n**`done` is required**: When you expect there to be next steps in an active proof.\n\n## Error Priority\n\nFix errors in this order — higher-priority errors make lower-priority ones unreliable:\n\n1. **Syntax errors** → 2. **Type errors** → 3. **Unsolved goals / tactic failures** → 4. **Linter warnings**\n\n\"Unsolved goals\" errors appear on `by` or `=>` lines, NOT where you add tactics. If there's an \"unsolved goals\" on line 59 but a tactic error on line 65 — fix line 65 FIRST.\n\nStop writing tactics after any error.\n\n## Work on the Hardest Case First\n\n### Across Theorems\n\nGo directly to the target theorem. Don't fill in `sorry`s in helper lemmas first — Lean treats `sorry` as an axiom, so dependent theorems still work.\n\nMove sorries earlier in the file by replacing a `sorry` proof with references to simpler lemmas:\n\n```lean\n-- Before:\ntheorem main_theorem : A = C := by sorry\n\n-- After:\ntheorem lemma1 : A = B := by sorry\ntheorem lemma2 : B = C := by sorry\ntheorem main_theorem : A = C := by\n  rw [lemma1, lemma2]\n```\n\n### Within a Proof\n\nWhen a proof has multiple cases, `sorry` the easy cases and work on the hardest one first. If the hard case fails, effort on easy cases is wasted.\n\n```lean\nmatch n with\n| 0 => sorry -- fill in later\n| 1 => sorry -- fill in later\n| n + 2 => -- WORK ON THIS FIRST\n```\n\n## Proof Cleanup\n\nAfter getting a proof to work, clean it up immediately:\n- Combine redundant steps (`rw [a]; rw [b]` → `rw [a, b]`)\n- Test if `simp` can handle more (remove earlier steps one by one)\n- Find the truly minimal proof\n\n## Dependent Type Rewriting Issues\n\n**When you encounter \"motive is not type correct\" or similar errors during rewriting:**\n\n### The Problem\n\nRewriting a term `b` that appears in dependent types (like `hab : a ≤ b`) fails because the motive cannot abstract over the dependencies.\n\n```lean\nhave hb : b = f x\nrw [hb]  -- Error: motive is not type correct\n```\n\n### The Solution: Generalize First, Instantiate Last\n\nProve a generalized statement for an arbitrary parameter, then instantiate:\n\n```lean\nsuffices ∀ s, statement_about s by\n  have h_specific := the_equality_you_have\n  convert this ?_ <;> exact h_specific\nintro s\n-- Now prove the general statement for arbitrary s\n```\n\nThis works because the generalized statement has no dependencies on the problematic term, and `convert` handles the dependent type coercions at the end.\n\n## Verification\n\nNever declare a proof complete while `sorry` placeholders or error diagnostics remain.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PLAN.md\nsed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,300p' aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\nrg --files work reviews aristotle_tasks AristotleCandidates | rg -i 'P60R|P60|handoff|status|closeout|audit' | sort\nsed -n '1,260p' reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\nsed -n '1,260p' aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PLAN.md\nsed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,300p' aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\nrg --files work reviews aristotle_tasks AristotleCandidates | rg -i 'P60R|P60|handoff|status|closeout|audit' | sort\nsed -n '1,260p' reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\nsed -n '1,260p' aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Active plan: two-lane stabilizer-algebra formalization\n\n## Decision — 2026-08-07\n\nThe project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\nstabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\nsilently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n\n### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n\nFor a general consistent stabilizer system and region, construct the decreasing\nlocal-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\ntracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\nand derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n\nThis lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\nseparate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\nof a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\nmerely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n\n### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n\nFrom a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\ntheir coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\nmodels, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\nthe special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n\n`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n\nAfter proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\ntrivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\nnot follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\nspatial factorization.\n\n### Reconnection\n\nLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\nconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\nthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\nthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\nthe two results remain logically independent.\n\n## Aristotle package sequence\n\n### Shared/central core\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n\n### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | After P55D, prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n\n### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n\n## Initial parallel wave\n\nSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\nand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   traciality and faithfulness.\n8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   integrated and audited.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n\n1. Split coordinate indices into pure and mixed sectors.\n2. Establish the infinite-product GNS factorization.\n3. Identify the pure sector as `B(K_pure)`.\n4. Identify the mixed sector as a finite matrix factor when finite, or the\nhyperfinite `II_1` factor when infinite.\n5. Establish the spatial tensor-product identification of the product\nrepresentation.\n\n**Gate D:** every analytic theorem is either formalized against a supported\nMathlib API or recorded as an exact external theorem with source locator and\nexplicit hypothesis.\n\n## Phase E — theorem and trace corollaries\n\n1. Transport the Phase-D product classification through the Phase-C GNS\nunitary to the regional von Neumann algebra.\n2. State the finite-pure and infinite-pure cases separately.\n3. Finite pure sector: derive the normalized tracial-state conclusion.\n4. Infinite pure sector: state the faithful normal semifinite trace/weight\nconclusion; do not call it a tracial state.\n5. Audit every conclusion against `main.tex:1740-1752` and record any required\nmanuscript correction separately.\n\n## Parallelization\n\nUntil Phase B is blocked on a single coherent-coordinate construction, run in\nparallel:\n\n- finite phase/cocycle verification;\n- finite adapted-coordinate/stabilizer-state verification;\n- finite inclusion/coherence lemmas;\n- Mathlib/API feasibility audits for C-star inductive limits and GNS products;\n- product mixed-sector classification/source work.\n\nDo not parallelize mutually dependent attempts at the same global `alpha`.\nEach new Aristotle packet must use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` and state its\nsource basis plus every auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Exit criterion\n\nCall the manuscript theorem formally established only when Gates A--D are\ndischarged and Phase E compiles without substituting supplied interfaces for\nthe central finite-coordinate, C-star-extension, state-identity, or\nproduct-classification claims.\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n# P60R — standard positive-cone semifiniteness for the full-corner weight\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** repair the optional Lane-G global-weight theorem.\n  This packet makes no new manuscript claim and does not alter the accepted\n  no-central-type-III result of P51.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P60R`; Lane `G` optional recovery.\n- **Predecessors:** `P51`, `P50U`, both integrated and locally audited.\n  The existing `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` is an unaccepted P60 recovery\n  baseline, not a semantic predecessor: every declaration it is reused for\n  must remain locally compiled and be rechecked in this packet.\n- **Gate discharged:** prove the standard positive-cone semifiniteness of the\n  explicitly constructed global extended-positive trace under the same named\n  countable comparison-family hypothesis.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no claim that fullness alone produces the\n  comparison family/global weight, no direct-integral theorem, no Lane-H\n  factorization, and no assertion that a compression certificate by itself is\n  standard semifiniteness.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nEdit only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`.\n\nThe current `globalWeight_semifinite` proves that finite comparison projections\ngive finite compressions. Replace the exported use of that certificate by a\nstandard positive-cone predicate, for example:\n\n`∀ x ∈ M, x.IsPositive → x ≠ 0 → ∃ y ∈ M,\n  y.IsPositive ∧ y ≠ 0 ∧ y ≤ x ∧ globalWeight q Ω v y < ⊤`.\n\nDefine the weight's public domain to be positive elements of `M` (or an\nequivalent proved subtype/API), and formulate additivity, homogeneity,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, and semifiniteness there. The extended\nweight must not be presented as a linear functional on arbitrary operators.\n\nFor a nonzero positive `x`, construct its positive square root/factorization\ninside the concrete von Neumann algebra, `x = a^* a`, using the pinned Mathlib\ncontinuous functional calculus or new locally proved C-star lemmas. With the\nfinite comparison projection `p_N`, use\n\n`y_N = a^* p_N a`.\n\nProve that some `y_N` is nonzero, `y_N` is positive, `y_N ≤ x`, and\n`globalWeight q Ω v y_N < ⊤`; derive finite weight from the existing tracial\nlaw and the finite compression `p_N (a a^*) p_N`. The result may continue to\nassume `ComparisonFamily`; construction of that family from fullness remains a\nseparate unproved sigma-finite comparison theorem.\n\nRepair the exported bundle and `full_finite_corner_globalized_weight` so they\nstate only laws actually proved. Retain the current useful compression theorem\nunder an honest name rather than deleting it.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nNo new positive-square-root, factorization, order-density, normality,\nfaithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness field may be added. Use only the\nexisting explicit `ComparisonFamily`, P51/P50U hypotheses, and facts proved in\nthis file. If pinned Mathlib lacks a needed CFC fact, develop the smallest\nlocal lemma; do not replace it with an axiom or a supplied interface.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nEdit only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`; retain the\ncurrent imports or add the precise Mathlib CFC/order import needed for a proved\npositive square root. Do not modify P51, P50U, the manuscript, or unrelated\nfiles.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.FullCornerSemifiniteWeight` passes.\n- The standard positive-cone semifiniteness theorem has the literal nonzero\n  positive subelement/order-below conclusion above (or a formally equivalent\n  standard definition), not merely finite compressions.\n- The square-root/factorization and order inequality are proved, with no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, new axiom, or new supplied interface.\n- The response reports exact declarations, imports, commands, the retained\n  comparison-family assumption, and confirms the P51 provenance correction.\naristotle_tasks/P42-regional-theorem-contract-audit.md\naristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\naristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P39-state-preserving-gns-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport-closeout.md\nreviews/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary-closeout.md\nreviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md\nreviews/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower-closeout.md\nreviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\nreviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\nreviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\nreviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\nreviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\nreviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\nreviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\nreviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\nreviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md\nreviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\nreviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-closeout.md\nreviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\nreviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\n# P60 closeout review — full-corner semifinite weight\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: partial and blocked; do not advance Lane G.**\n\nThe exact archive\n`aristotle_responses/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-94c2fd67-fdc0344a.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only into its task-specific quarantine directory.  Its SHA-256 is\n`d52b56d1d7dcf36a90e96e89db6037aee25fa50cd82b36d7e68bf6ebdcade81b`.\nOnly the packet-authorized candidate\n`AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` was integrated into the\nlive tree; its quarantine and live SHA-256 is\n`1a1d0a592a2d2445d3a3905104f90b1214bb9bb3d3d36e5acc4750811b4a598b`.\nNo build, update, or dependency fetch was run in quarantine.\n\nThe candidate compiles and contains a substantial conditional construction,\nbut the packet's stated mathematical target is not fully met. The only\nacceptance blocker is the mismatch between its compression certificate and\nstandard positive-cone semifiniteness; the P51 predecessor correction is\nrecorded below.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe candidate defines `srcProj`, `rngProj`, `partialProj`, and the explicit\ncomparison-family structure at lines 110–145.  Its assumptions are:\n\n- `ComparisonFamily M q v`: `v n ∈ M`, idempotent source projections below\n  `q`, pairwise orthogonal range projections, strong convergence of the finite\n  range sums to `1`, and `srcProj v 0 = rngProj v 0 = q` (lines 128–145);\n- P50U's `IsFaithfulUltraweakNormalTracialCorner M q Ω`; and\n- `q Ω = Ω` for faithfulness (the exported theorem at lines 1123–1133).\n\nThe global definition is `globalWeight` (lines 280–290), the series of\n`ENNReal.ofReal` transported corner vector traces.  The principal proved\ndeclarations are `globalWeight_add`, `globalWeight_smul`, and\n`globalWeight_mono` (lines 352–385); `globalWeight_tracial` (lines 494–524);\n`globalWeight_faithful` (lines 540–601); the ultraweak and strong\nmonotone-supremum certificates\n`globalWeight_iSup_of_ultraweakTendsto` and\n`globalWeight_iSup_of_stronglyTendsto` (lines 648–705 and 672–705);\n`globalWeight_partialProj` and `globalWeight_corner` (lines 731–833); and\n`globalWeight_semifinite` (lines 903–926).  These are collected in\n`IsGlobalFaithfulNormalSemifiniteTrace` and\n`full_corner_global_semifinite_weight` (lines 1071–1133).\n\nThe missing comparison theorem is not silently assumed: the reduction\n`exists_comparisonFamily_of_orthogonal_decomposition` (lines 942–1001) still\nrequires the orthogonal decomposition and Murray–von Neumann comparison data.\nThe P51 wrapper `full_finite_corner_globalized_weight` (lines 1158–1175) also\nrequires the full P51 input data and an explicit comparison family.\n\n## Classification\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The extended-positive series definition; the displayed additivity, positive homogeneity, traciality, faithfulness, finite-partial-sum, corner-restriction, and monotone-supremum certificates compile from explicit premises. |\n| partial | The exported normality statement is a project-local quadratic-form/sequence certificate: it does not explicitly require positive elements or state the full standard normal-weight interface. |\n| partial | The declaration named `globalWeight_semifinite` proves finite compressions by an increasing strongly exhaustive family, but it does not state the standard semifiniteness condition on the positive cone (finite-weight positive subelements/order-density for every positive element). Its final claim “hence ... semifinite” is therefore stronger than the declaration actually establishes. |\n| corrected | P51 is accepted in `reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`; the original provenance objection consulted a superseded closeout. |\n| failed | None as a Lean compilation artifact; the candidate itself is not a failed build. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is therefore **not actually met at its stated\nscope**.  The candidate recovers a useful conditional weight-series and several\nvalid laws, but it does not discharge the standard semifiniteness gate.\n\n## Provenance correction — 2026-08-08\n\nThe predecessor objection in this review is superseded.  It consulted the\nhistorical rejected P51 closeout rather than the later accepted recovery\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`, whose decision\nis `advance`.  P51 is an accepted predecessor.  The P60 halt remains correct\nsolely because the candidate does not yet prove standard positive-cone\nsemifiniteness.  P60R is the approved focused recovery packet; it may revise\nthe candidate in place but must not weaken that missing theorem to a\ncompression-only certificate.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P60, Lane `G` optional strengthening — declared lane is\n  correct.\n- **Predecessors:** declared `P51`, `P50U`, both locally accepted in their\n  recovery/closeout reviews. The original P51 provenance objection is\n  superseded by the correction above.\n- **Permitted gate:** globalize a full finite corner to a faithful normal\n  semifinite weight under explicit comparison/countability hypotheses.  The\n  candidate reaches a conditional series construction and partial law\n  certificates, but not the standard semifiniteness conclusion.\n- **Forbidden claims:** respected.  It does not infer a global weight from\n  fullness alone, does not prove a direct-integral theorem, and makes no\n  Lane-H factorization or factor claim.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll Lean checks were run only in the already-built live project:\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.FullCornerSemifiniteWeight` — passed;\n- broader relevant build of P60 and P49–P51/P50U dependency modules — passed;\n- `lake build` — passed with zero new jobs;\n- `#print axioms` for `full_corner_global_semifinite_weight` and\n  `full_finite_corner_globalized_weight` — only `propext`, `Classical.choice`,\n  and `Quot.sound`;\n- forbidden-placeholder scan over P60 and its direct dependency chain — no\n  executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration (the only hit was\n  negative-scope prose in P49C);\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nCompilation and axiom reports do not establish the missing standard\nsemifiniteness interface.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nArtifact types: math, code, computation, and workflow.  The review checked the\ncomparison-family fields, the construction of `globalWeight`, the exported\ntheorem signatures, the normality hypotheses, the semifiniteness declaration,\nthe predecessor audit, and the forbidden-claim boundary. The remaining\nacceptance-blocking finding is the mismatch between the claimed standard\nsemifiniteness and the compression certificate; the P51 provenance finding was\nsubsequently corrected.\n\n## Cleanup and remaining state\n\nKept intentionally: the exact archive, its task-specific quarantine\nextraction, the integrated P60 candidate, and this review.  All unrelated\nmodified and untracked files were preserved.  No manuscript file was changed;\nthere was no commit, push, new Aristotle submission, archive build, dependency\nfetch, or destructive cleanup.\n\nThe queue has not advanced. P60R will preserve the accepted P51/P50U\npredecessors and prove a genuine standard positive-cone semifiniteness theorem;\nthe current compression result remains a local supporting certificate.\n# P60 — optional global semifinite weight from a full finite corner\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** optional strengthening beyond the Lane-G manuscript\n  conclusion; this packet makes no claim that the manuscript requires it.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P60`; Lane `G` optional strengthening.\n- **Predecessors:** `P51`, `P50U`, both integrated and locally audited before\n  submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** globalize a full finite corner to a faithful normal\n  semifinite weight under exact comparison/countability hypotheses.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no claim that P51 already supplied a global\n  weight, no direct-integral theorem, and no Lane-H factorization.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`. Use P51's\nfull finite corner and P50U's literally ultraweak-normal faithful tracial\ncorner state. Under an explicit normalized countable comparison family of\npartial isometries whose source projections lie below `q`, whose pairwise\northogonal range projections sum strongly to `1`, and whose distinguished\nzeroth member has source and range projection `q`, define the ambient\nextended-positive trace/weight on the positive cone with values in `ℝ≥0∞` by\nthe corresponding monotone series of transported corner traces. Develop the\nsmallest project-local extended-positive-weight API required when pinned\nMathlib does not provide one.\n\nProve, from the displayed construction, additivity, positive homogeneity,\ntraciality, faithfulness, normality in the standard weight sense (preservation\nof suprema of increasing positive nets/sequences at the level supported by the\ndeveloped API), and semifiniteness. The global extended-valued weight is not a\nbounded linear functional, so do not define its normality as ordinary\nultraweak continuity on all of `M`; instead use P50U's ultraweak-normal bounded\ncorner functional to prove the monotone-supremum law. Also prove the value on\nfinite partial sums and that the global weight restricts exactly to the P50U\ntrace on `q M q`. Keep the separate theorem that fullness plus the exact\nsigma-finite comparison theorem produces the required countable family; if\nthat comparison theorem itself is unavailable, take only the countable family\nas a named hypothesis and do not claim it follows from fullness.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList every comparison-family, orthogonality, normalization, and convergence\npremise explicitly. Normality,\nfaithfulness, traciality, and semifiniteness of the resulting weight are proof\ntargets, not permitted premise fields. The P50U corner normality theorem must\nbe used rather than the older WOT field name. Do not encode the desired global\nweight itself as an interface field or axiom.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean`; import P51\nand P50U.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.FullCornerSemifiniteWeight` succeeds without\nforbidden declarations and reports the exact optional assumptions, the weight\ndefinition, and the declarations proving its required weight laws. A\ngenuine missing comparison theorem may remain conditional; the weight laws may\nnot be replaced by a bundled assumption.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
