{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\nsed -n '1,220p' reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\nsed -n '1,240p' work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nsed -n '1,220p' work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\nprintf '\\\\n-- archive --\\\\n'\nsha256sum aristotle_responses/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-ae5ca7f3-9cf226e6.tar.gz\ntar -tzf aristotle_responses/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-ae5ca7f3-9cf226e6.tar.gz\nprintf '\\\\n-- quarantine before --\\\\n'\nfind aristotle_responses/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-ae5ca7f3-9cf226e6-quarantine -maxdepth 2 -printf '%y %p\\\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort || true\nprintf '\\\\n-- live candidate status --\\\\n'\nsha256sum AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\nrg -n \\\"globalWeight_semifinite|Standard|semifinite|sorry|admit|axiom|opaque|unsafe|full_finite_corner_globalized_weight|full_corner_global_semifinite_weight\\\" AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\"","aggregated_output":"# P51 recovery review — full finite corner and central type-III exclusion\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: accepted after correcting the packet's manuscript source range; Lane G may advance.**\n\nThe first closeout correctly quarantined the candidate because the packet cited\nonly `main.tex:1456-1536`, omitting the finite-corner argument it used.  The\nauthoritative manuscript contains the complete relevant chain at\n`main.tex:1418-1539`: the finite-projection corollary and proof at lines\n1422-1445, its abstract lemma at 1447-1450, fullness at 1473-1499, and the\ncentral-summand theorem and proof at 1501-1539.  The packet and integrated\ncandidate now cite that full range.  The rejected closeout remains preserved in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md`.\n\nThe exact task-specific archive was\n`aristotle_responses/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-10f2fe5c-f7631f0b.tar.gz`.\nIts candidate was extracted only in the task-specific quarantine directory and\nhad SHA-256\n`99294408c47f35f5716520b2a423fc399f6957bab6c632a184e5aa5daa75264c`.\nOnly `AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` was integrated.\nAfter correcting documentation locators, its live SHA-256 is\n`448540c487d612be26c66a70e05927d765dd8f4c90d1e8420c29b70cad981317`;\nno proof term or declaration type was changed.\n\n## Exact checked conclusions\n\n- `isFiniteProjection_of_faithfulNormalTracialCorner` proves that the P50\n  faithful tracial corner functional makes `q` a finite projection of `M`.\n- `isFull_of_dense_cyclic_vectors` proves fullness from complement commutation,\n  `q Omega = Omega`, and density of the vectors `b a Omega`.\n- `central_summand_nonzero_finite_projection` produces the explicit projection\n  `z * q`, proves it nonzero and finite in `M`, places it in `z M`, and proves\n  its finiteness relative to that summand.\n- `not_isTypeIIILike_centralSummand` derives the project-local type-III\n  obstruction.\n- `full_finite_corner_central_exclusion` exports the conditional Lane-G result\n  from the P50 finite-system, represented-algebra, commutation, and density\n  premises.\n\nThe proof of finiteness uses P50's traciality and faithfulness fields, not its\nfield currently named `normal`.  Therefore the separately tracked need to\nformalize the standard ultraweak definition of normality does not invalidate\nP51's finite-projection or central-summand conclusions.\n\n## Scope and remaining assumptions\n\nThe result is conditional on the same explicit inputs as P50: the compatible\nfinite codespace system and decreasing tower, the norm-closed represented\nregional algebra with the stated finite-stage density data, complement\ncommutation, and the dense-vector premise.  It constructs no global trace or\nweight.  `IsTypeIIILike` is a project-local set-relative obstruction predicate;\nthe module does not formalize direct integrals, trivial center, Lane-H tensor\nfactorization, or the complete external classification theory of type III\nvon Neumann algebras.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion` — passed.\n- Axiom audit of the four declarations named above — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan — no executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`,\n  `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration.\n- Source audit against the authoritative manuscript — the corrected range\n  `main.tex:1418-1539` covers every manuscript-facing claim used by P51.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking defect remains.  The proof produces a nonzero finite\nprojection, rather than merely a finite-dimensional subalgebra, in every\nnonzero central summand.  Its conditional hypotheses and its project-local\ntype-III obstruction remain explicit.  The ultraweak-normality bridge is a\nseparate mandatory infrastructure package and is not silently claimed here.\n\nAUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes\n\nAUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance\n# P50U closeout review — ultraweak topology and normality bridge\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: accepted; shared infrastructure gate discharged and the queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe exact task archive\n`aristotle_responses/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-665c01eb-43682f4c.tar.gz`\nwas extracted only into its task-specific quarantine directory.  No build,\nupdate, or dependency fetch was run there.  The sole packet-authorized module,\n`AristotleCandidates/UltraweakNormality.lean`, was reviewed and integrated\ninto the live project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`ce7d0887c340c4f1209d8f88aa05a556b77f2763bb4d2ce0392ca768bb3b8997`\nboth in quarantine and live.\n\nThe packet's P50 predecessor is locally accepted: the recovery closeout records\nthe provenance repair for P49 and the accepted P50 recovery, whose live\n`NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` hash is\n`2e9f93915721cf61978bd718ff972c3d0c26c8662efdc03fe7b91b65a627def2`.\nIts exported `normal_faithful_corner_trace` invokes P49's\n`D.finite_corner_trace` and P49C, rather than accepting cyclicity or density\nas an interface field.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe integrated module defines:\n\n- `UltraweakCoeff`, with sequences `x : Nat -> H`,\n  `y : Nat -> H ->L[C] C`, and\n  `Summable (fun n => ||x n|| * ||y n||)`;\n- `UltraweakCLM`, a type copy of bounded operators with the topology induced\n  by all `UltraweakCoeff.eval` series;\n- `UltraweakCLM.continuous_toWOT`, using\n  `UltraweakCoeff.single x y` to make each WOT matrix coefficient an\n  ultraweak generator;\n- `IsUltraweaklyContinuous.of_wot`,\n  `cornerTau_ultraweakContinuous`, and\n  `IsFaithfulUltraweakNormalTracialCorner`; and\n- `ultraweak_normal_faithful_corner_trace`, which exports P50's corner\n  theorem with a literal ultraweak-continuity normality field.\n\nNo new premise of ultraweak continuity, normality, separability,\nfinite-dimensionality, supplied predual, supplied topology comparison, or\nglobal trace/weight is added.  The final theorem is conditional exactly on\nP50's explicit finite-codespace, decreasing-tower, represented-algebra,\ncommuting-complement, and dense-vector inputs.  These remain external to the\nmanuscript-specific stabilizer realization; P50U is infrastructure only.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The ultraweak topology is induced by arbitrary absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, not aliased to WOT, SOT, or norm topology.  The checked identity `UltraweakCLM.continuous_toWOT` has the required direction, and composition proves the WOT-to-ultraweak continuity bridge. |\n| partial | The exported corner theorem is conditional on the already explicit P50 hypotheses; it does not construct the represented stabilizer system, complement, or dense-vector premise from the manuscript. |\n| blocked | None at the P50U infrastructure gate. |\n| failed | None.  The candidate meets the packet's stated acceptance criteria. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated infrastructure scope.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P50U, lane `shared` — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P50 is integrated, compiled, and accepted in\n  `reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md`; P49 and P49C are\n  likewise accepted in the local recovery/closeout chain.\n- **Gate discharged:** the standard ultraweak topology, the continuous identity\n  from ultraweak to WOT, and the literal ultraweak-normal P50 export.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module adds no traciality or\n  faithfulness proof, finite-projection/fullness result, central type-III\n  exclusion, global trace/weight, or Lane-H tensor-factor/factor theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll Lean commands were run in the already-built live project:\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UltraweakNormality` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.FiniteCornerTrace\n  AristotleCandidates.NormalFaithfulCornerTrace\n  AristotleCandidates.KaplanskyDensity AristotleCandidates.UltraweakNormality`\n  — passed (one pre-existing non-blocking style suggestion in\n  `KaplanskyDensity.lean:463`).\n- `lake build` — passed.\n- `#print axioms` for `continuous_toWOT`, `of_wot`,\n  `cornerTau_ultraweakContinuous`, and\n  `ultraweak_normal_faithful_corner_trace` — each lists only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-placeholder scan of P50U and its direct dependency chain — no\n  executable `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration; the sole scan hit is\n  negative-scope documentation in P49C.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review and cleanup\n\nArtifact types: math and workflow.  The review checked the topology direction,\nthat arbitrary summable series occur in the definition, the one-term WOT\ngenerator argument, the exact P50 export hypotheses, and the forbidden-claim\nboundary.  No acceptance-blocking defect was found.  Compilation and axiom\nreports do not establish the remaining manuscript-specific P50 premises.\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P50U candidate, its exact raw archive and\nquarantine extraction, and this review.  All pre-existing modified and\nuntracked files remain preserved; no manuscript file was changed, and no\ncommit, push, remote submission, archive build, update, or dependency fetch\noccurred.\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\n\n-- archive --\nb1aa1b1f547a45608fe338978bdd396a41326b7f755e2cb562b6fc7c06559306  aristotle_responses/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair-ae5ca7f3-9cf226e6.tar.gz\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/lakefile.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/Formalization.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/lean-toolchain\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/lake-manifest.json\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p60r-7kr05gwd_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/DensityPartialTrace.lean\naristotle