6.9.3(i), printed p. 132/PDF p. 141; Kadison--Ringrose I §4.2, printed p. 245/PDF p. 254. [Task 3]\n  2474\t- If `z` is central and `q` is a projection, then `r=(1-z)q` is a projection: `r^*=q(1-z)=(1-z)q=r` and `r^2=(1-z)^2q^2=r`. Thus `q-zq=r>=0`, proving `zq<=q`. If `zq=0`, then `q=(1-z)q`, so `c_M(q)<=1-z<1`, contradicting fullness `c_M(q)=1`. [Task 4]\n  2475\t- The ambient-corner bridge is exact, not an inclusion shortcut: `(zq)M_Gamma(zq)=(zq)(zM_Gamma)(zq)`. Apply the corner-finiteness lemma in ambient `zM_Gamma` to `p=zq`; the restricted object is a faithful positive tracial functional, not necessarily a normalized state. Blackadar III.1.1.5 (printed p. 237/PDF p. 245) supplies central carrier/support; do not conflate it with C*-ideal “full corner.” [Task 5]\n  2476\t- Nielsen--Chuang calls Clifford gates “normalizer gates”: §10.5.2 Eq. (10.87), PDF p. 493/printed p. 459, and Theorem 10.6, PDF p. 495/printed p. 461, support Clifford-generated stabilizer states. It does not state the general flat-reduced-spectrum theorem; derive it from the stabilizer projector (Prop. 10.5/Eq. 10.85) and partial trace (§2.4.3), yielding `rho_F=P_F/rank(P_F)`. [Task 6]\n  2477\t- If `c_n -> c` in norm, then `||c_n^*c_n-c^*c|| <= (||c_n||+||c||)||c_n-c|| -> 0`; a bounded extension `omega` is norm-continuous, so `omega(c^*c)=lim omega(c_n^*c_n)>=0`. Kadison--Ringrose I §3.1 Definition 3.1.1, PDF p. 183/printed p. 174, gives submultiplicativity and the preceding paragraph states multiplication is jointly continuous. [Task 7]\n  2478\t- The state-existence pilot is `research/state_existence_argument.json` plus `research/argument_artifact.schema.json` and `research/validate_argument_artifact.py`; validation reported 8 objects, 7 statements, 6 steps, 3 review gaps. Semantic dependencies are canonical; Lamport hierarchy is a derived rendering. Keep the graph as provenance/navigation, with the finite-enclosure, Hermitian/phase, and positivity/compatibility gaps propagated as `conditional`. [Task 8]\n  2479\t\n  2480\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  2481\t\n  2482\t- symptom: standalone dictated fragment does not compile -> cause: inherited macros such as `\\L`, `\\D`, `\\id`, `\\supp` are undefined -> fix: provide a wrapper with every required notation macro before compiling. [Task 1]\n  2483\t- symptom: proof says the corner state is faithful -> cause: the faithfulness proof remains commented out -> fix: state only the active, checked conclusion of normal traciality until faithfulness is proved and enabled. [Task 1]\n  2484\t- symptom: tracial extension is claimed from vector limits alone -> cause: product convergence and net indexing were omitted -> fix: state bounded strong convergence for both `X_kY_k\\to XY` and `Y_kX_k\\to YX`, with the common product-directed set; do not switch nets to sequences without metrizability. [Task 1]\n  2485\t- symptom: finiteness is inferred from a merely semifinite trace -> cause: finite value on the corner identity was not checked -> fix: require a faithful trace with `tau(p)<infinity` and include the `v=pvp` transfer from `pMp` to `M`. [Task 2]\n  2486\t- symptom: positivity of a product of commuting projections is asserted before the order inequality is established -> cause: the projection calculation was skipped -> fix: prove self-adjointness and idempotence of `(1-z)q`, then use `q-zq=(1-z)q>=0`. [Task 4]\n  2487\t- symptom: `zq` is called finite in `zM_Gamma` merely because `(zq)M_Gamma(zq)` is a subalgebra -> cause: upward finiteness was inferred from arbitrary inclusion -> fix: state the exact corner identity and invoke the corner-finiteness lemma with the named ambient algebra. [Task 5]\n  2488\t- symptom: Nielsen--Chuang is cited as directly proving flat reduced spectra -> cause: its projector and partial-trace ingredients were mistaken for an explicit general theorem -> fix: label the normalized-projector conclusion as an additional derivation or find a source that states it. [Task 6]\n  2